  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "Let \\(ABCD\\) be a trapezoid with the measure of base \\(AB\\) twice that of base \\(DC,\\) and let \\(E\\) be the point of intersection of the diagonals. If the measure of diagonal \\(AC\\) is \\(11,\\) then that of segment \\(EC\\) is equal to:",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(3\\frac23\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(3\\frac34\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(4\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(3\\frac12\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(3\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "a",
    "value": "11/3"
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1972-p18.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Since \\(AB\\parallel DC,\\) triangles \\(ABE\\) and \\(CDE\\) are similar. Hence \\[ AE:EC=AB:DC=2:1. \\] Thus \\(AC=AE+EC=3EC=11,\\) so \\[ EC=\\frac{11}{3}=3\\frac23. \\]\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is A.",
      "hints": [
        "Triangles \\(ABE\\) and \\(CDE\\) are similar",
        "The base ratio \\(AB:DC=2:1\\) also equals \\(AE:EC\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
